<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:04:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France braces for fresh protests in test for Macron's policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b48b344d29b0a91d7797241c94f4fd0a676e9db70d33dd14021174b1d6698f8f</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T06:24:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-fresh-protests-in-test-for-macron-s-policies--b95d857778a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-fresh-protests-in-test-for-macron-s-policies" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of protesters are expected to march through French cities and public workers to strike on Thursday, in a fresh test for President Emmanuel Macron after weeks of ​unrest that have rattled ‌his government and dominated the agenda five months ahead of a presidential election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: France braces for nationwide strikes in fresh test for Macron’s policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04ecfc0455c012c500b21ce4a99cdde9ae67733b0b03a88c2369719723cd9d90</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T05:53:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261105-live-france-nationwide-strikes-living-costs--b8adf3b2e07a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261105-live-france-nationwide-strikes-living-costs" /><summary type="html">Strikes and demonstrations are planned across France on Thursday, with trade unions urging the government to support households struggling with rising living costs. The nationwide action follows weeks of social unrest. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Melania Trump to host Ukrainian, Russian officials at White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dff4e202b8e53d7aa5b79791e2cfd53da59b6457702d5cab307c664ce10b1fb</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T05:23:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-melania-trump-to-host-ukrainian-russian-officials-at-white-house--000b54c4acdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-melania-trump-to-host-ukrainian-russian-officials-at-white-house" /><summary type="html">Delegations of Russian and Ukrainian officials, including human rights chiefs from both countries, are set to meet with US First Lady Melania Trump at the White House Thursday ahead of talks in Abu Dhabi aimed at ending the Ukraine war. It comes weeks after Melania Trump helped broker a partial ceasefire that enabled the evacuation of civilians from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong gets 10 more years in jail for foreign collusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbab21d3a82516e9feab8183bf56acc5a4903fa6d9cd333476e93be15cb72da2</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T03:31:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion--961948348fab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in prison on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, a court summary said. Wong, 30, pleaded guilty in September to seeking foreign sanctions against Hong Kong and China under Beijing’s national security law, having spent nearly six years imprisoned.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea to deploy military mission to keep Strait of Hormuz open</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:244ebb9b129eb23a33d2fa572a570f9dd952cc0d81ad6ce4fce2f1133d9212bc</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T02:17:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz--37e442fe8805.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">South Korea will deploy maritime patrol aircraft and an explosive ordnance disposal team near the Strait of Hormuz to help keep the waterway open, its defence ministry said Thursday. Seoul said it would protect commercial shipping and energy supplies while ruling out military intervention in the ongoing US-Iran war.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Champions League: Real Madrid seal late comeback as Liverpool lose to Fenerbahce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d380eb35da786d084b4ab02df3955e82bc5eae9f8cf706c99821812e5f9f57a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T22:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261104-champions-league-real-madrid-comeback-liverpool-fenerbahce--948306043957.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261104-champions-league-real-madrid-comeback-liverpool-fenerbahce" /><summary type="html">Real Madrid maintained their perfect Champions League record as Federico Valverde’s stoppage-time strike secured a 3-2 comeback win at AEK Athens on Wednesday. Madrid twice trailed before Valverde scored from long range in the 92nd minute. Liverpool’s winning start ended with a surprise 3-2 defeat at Fenerbahce in the competition.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu claims 'serious concerns' of foreign spending to sway Israeli election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21c0eefe47f4a72819b6ab4a05f9601af8d6dd11c17aca8fb75c823be269d53e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election--38bacb102ad6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Wednesday cited "serious suspicions" around foreign interference in Israel's recent parliamentary elections. He claims foreign countries spent large amounts of money to influence the results, while the largest Arab-Israeli bloc called such accusations "political persecution".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>South Africans vote in key municipal elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57725a49f333927d5a84ad55358db26392d06b489ac8b7bc56b6d7717ad10e1d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-key-municipal-elections--157bcd2b0585.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-key-municipal-elections" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, a crucial test for South Africa's  ruling ANC as millions vote to elect municipal governments. Also, Ethiopia has expelled six Sudanese diplomats amid accusations it's allowing the paramilitary RSF to launch drone strikes from its territory. And a deepening humanitarian crisis in Ethiopia, where renewed fighting has displaced thousands.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Musk-backed candidates lose midterms despite financial backing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b990a680a8675926ddb86f1f0b1081e4c36c61b8f2194eb2f49b63def00186f0</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:06:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/musk-backed-candidates-lose-midterms-despite-financial-backing--30bf6b2544d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/musk-backed-candidates-lose-midterms-despite-financial-backing" /><summary type="html">Shares of Tesla and SpaceX dropped after the Democratic party swept to power in America's midterm elections. Their founder, tech titan Elon Musk, poured over $440 million into Republican candidates and causes, the single biggest campaign donor in the election cycle. But his investment fell flat, as his preferred candidates lost races in Texas, where he has put down roots.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trump’s second-term playbook: Fake news, AI and attacks on his critics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af6bd97788d6a0062458be60cc49981d5adeae55dfe9513bab8402c840eed932</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:44:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261104-trump-s-second-term-playbook-fake-news-ai-and-attacks-on-his-critics--e29038ea0d3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261104-trump-s-second-term-playbook-fake-news-ai-and-attacks-on-his-critics" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump could be credited with popularising the term "fake news", but his own presidency has been riddled with numerous false claims, conspiracy theories and misleading content. In this special fact-checking segment, Vedika Bahl examines his Trump's second term: his consistent attacks on political opponents, use of AI-generated images to glorify himself and push political narratives, and what happens when journalists challenge him.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>How Chinese AI is censoring the controversy around Mbappé’s Chairman Mao comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0eb50798ed6707cf3c8646ddf420caeb1dcc92698ba61fe0720ab51a729e27b5</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments--925db7d6d62f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments" /><summary type="html">Footballer Kylian Mbappé sparked a wave of condemnation across China when he implied that Chinese leader Mao Zedong was a dictator. In China, information about this controversy is being censored by Chinese AI chatbots.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Blue wave across America: do US midterms signal beginning of the end for Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:032586f39d08902b36e0e3bca1ff1fbc7f8b13e7d481500862a9c5b3a6f9e30a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:49:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261104-blue-wave-across-america-do-us-midterms-signal-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump--f1d9ca650a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261104-blue-wave-across-america-do-us-midterms-signal-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump" /><summary type="html">He asked voters to pretend he was on the ballot and they did. Voters across the United States chasing Donald Trump's Republican majorities from both houses of Congress. How big a landslide for the Democrats?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Trump says going to war in Iran was worth it, despite midterm rout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a29c0056bf012154284136d90e7af443c843bd47bc23315dc87929107a2bd1f</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:32:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats warn Trump camp to ‘lawyer up’ as anger over corruption drives midterms wipeout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c06deaa4c90eac46709a75df493d5e468b20e6d9c98f42c97b03d47caba6174</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:01:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-democrats-warn-trump-camp-lawyer-up-anger-over-corruption-drives-midterms-wipeout-gop--7b31d5ddc778.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-democrats-warn-trump-camp-lawyer-up-anger-over-corruption-drives-midterms-wipeout-gop" /><summary type="html">Corruption in government was high on the minds of US voters as they dealt US President Donald Trump’s party a chastening defeat in midterm elections, toppling Republican strongholds like dominoes and flipping both chambers of Congress. Triumphant Democrats have warned the Trump administration to “lawyer up”; how they go about tackling alleged graft and abuse of power could shape both their own fortunes and the country’s politics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Once-in-a-generation event: Historic election a shocking repudiation of Trump &amp; the MAGA movement'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35be95ae0ba79a12d57e3a5e028007eed5fdbbfd6849755fb833dcbc172e1d66</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:49:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/once-in-a-generation-event-historic-election-a-shocking-repudiation-of-trump-the-maga-movement--e99c6f8b95fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/once-in-a-generation-event-historic-election-a-shocking-repudiation-of-trump-the-maga-movement" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Adam Jentleson, President of the Searchlight Institute and author of Supermajority: How Democrats Can Build Lasting Power, For Jentleson, the Democrats' sweeping midterm victory represents far more than the familiar backlash against an incumbent president. "This is a once-in-a-generation event." But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? "Pluralism is not just a political strategy. It is actually a moral good in a democracy," he insists. But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? And can a party united by opposition to Trump sustain that unity when confronted with difficult choices over healthcare, immigration, economic inequality and climate change?</summary></entry><entry><title>European leaders welcome Democrats' US midterms election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8680ec91f3183c20193a82172ee8bf04cb0cb2a8c8f5265ebbdb84257131fe7a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:00:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win--9eb298186d7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win" /><summary type="html">European leaders voiced hopes for a reset with the United States on Wednesday, November 4, after voters delivered a huge midterm election defeat to President Donald Trump and his Republican party. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d88e60c4962c3a7c6455e3628cf8c75dae51308893c81cdfae3aeb450d821e3</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-bring-a-wave-of-historic-firsts-as-minorities-win-key-races--466ff9f5f4fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-bring-a-wave-of-historic-firsts-as-minorities-win-key-races" /><summary type="html">US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races: The first Native American female senator in Minnesota, the first openly gay male senator in New Hampshire, the first Muslim senator in Michigan and the country's first Black female governor in Georgia. FRANCE 24's Elitsa Gadeva has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Iran's deputy parliament speaker reacts to Trump's elections setback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ed57901f74b88becb1c640aec8917bd7758989ff52d0be473e737d3610a577e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:50:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1--b3baa850b100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1" /><summary type="html">First Deputy Speaker of the Parliament of Iran Ali Nikzad on Wednesday attributed Republican losses in the US midterm elections to Washington's war with Iran, telling lawmakers that American efforts to pressure Tehran had failed.  Democrats won control of both chambers of Congress in Tuesday's midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer on US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7fb0c09fc4fd4de53fffb0fd15502f4b493039d6d8c76f2d8b2c012d35e5cb7</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:04:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-senate-democratic-leader-chuck-schumer-on-us-midterms--86de370c3725.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-senate-democratic-leader-chuck-schumer-on-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">The US Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer talked to the press after the midterm election results. Democrats are riding their sweep of Congress into a new era, eager to meet voter demands for change with plans to tackle high costs of living and confront President Donald Trump's final years in the White House.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: How will Trump manage working with Democrats?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6fdd55fb89ad4e2b69f3b28fe8ea304d8fab9bd41a747436f3d8ea7cb324650</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:04:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:24:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-how-will-trump-manage-working-with-democrats--595e74419046.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-how-will-trump-manage-working-with-democrats" /><summary type="html">Democrats are riding their sweep of Congress into a new era, eager to meet voter demands for change with plans to tackle high costs of living. How will Donald Trump manage to work with them? FRANCE 24's Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tale of 2 midterms: Republican redistricting 'backfired' while Democrats 'exceeded all expectations'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dca5decba509c6b4eebcfa21bcbd86aac223e8df0c9b454dfc8e265308dea2b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:04:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tale-of-2-midterms-republican-redistricting-backfired-while-democrats-exceeded-all-expectations--e3ed6aa1e437.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tale-of-2-midterms-republican-redistricting-backfired-while-democrats-exceeded-all-expectations" /><summary type="html">Following a resounding Midterm election defeat, Is MAGA Losing Its Grip on the Republican Party? Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bryan Lanza, Republican strategist and Partner in Mercury's Washington DC office. "The big thing about MAGA was confrontation, in your face," explained Lanza. But following a veritable blue wave, he believes the electorate has delivered a warning: "We need to move beyond that." While Donald Trump has acknowledged the Democratic victory, at times combative, at times conciliatory, Lanza argues that the president must begin his final two years in office reversing damaging tariffs, addressing widespread dissatisfaction with immigration enforcement and navigating a highly unpopular Iran war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump after the midterms: Gridlock, impeachment and succession?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a06497890cb6dcb5c6084c25c5dffa47b51899b01302bacd02da4225989dc3b1</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:54:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-trump-after-the-midterms-gridlock-impeachment-and-succession--6a13fd719356.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-trump-after-the-midterms-gridlock-impeachment-and-succession" /><summary type="html">Following the US midterms, US President Donald Trump could face a turbulent final two years in office. From budget battles to potential impeachment proceedings, what does the new political balance of power mean for his presidency? FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle breaks it down.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: 'Maybe the best colour for Texas is purple'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f7a4e6c59df91a7ccfc6bfc481eb9f96b3705a08269ff94bac600f1690f9183</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:04:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-maybe-the-best-colour-for-texas-is-purple--208d404b28e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-maybe-the-best-colour-for-texas-is-purple" /><summary type="html">Texas flipped blue following the US midterm elections, marking a historic shift for a state that hasn't been led by Democrats in decades. The legacy of prolonged Republican leadership has left a lasting mark, but as Democrat James Talarico said with this election, 'maybe the best colour for Texas is purple.' FRANCE 24's Texas correspondent Andres Espinal reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Is Republican Party able to pivot away from MAGA movement, or will it sputter forward leaderless?'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:166a443e5bbe6f354acf0d2491715cefc72ced0e320e9a5b800784437e70d6f0</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:04:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:16:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/is-republican-party-able-to-pivot-away-from-maga-movement-or-will-it-sputter-forward-leaderless--65a3a2fd5e2f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/is-republican-party-able-to-pivot-away-from-maga-movement-or-will-it-sputter-forward-leaderless" /><summary type="html">Does an electoral repudiation of Donald Trump also mark the beginning of MAGA’s decline? Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Ian Reifowitz, SUNY Distinguished Professor of Historical Studies at Empire State University, who describes the Republican defeat as “an absolute and complete repudiation” of the president. He connects voters’ economic frustrations with resentment over presidential enrichment, while questioning whether ideological differences between progressive and moderate Democrats proved decisive. Looking towards 2028, Reifowitz identifies a central Republican dilemma: “If JD Vance is the nominee, he can’t run against Donald Trump”, yet Trump himself may refuse to relinquish control of the party.</summary></entry></feed>
